e time in and time out of multiple employees i.e. of a particular pay group for multiple days selected in the ")),o[12]||(o[12]=e("b",{style:{"mso-bidi-font-weight":"normal"}},"Time Card",-1)),o[13]||(o[13]=v(" screen.")),s(c)])]),o[47]||(o[47]=Zo('<h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138443"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.2</span></span>Multiple Swipe </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> This option is provided to display multiple logs in and logs out time of an employee in a day in the time card screen. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When the user enables this setting, either of the following options can be selected: </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Allow Swipe Code </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Consider FirstIn LastOut </p><h4>Allow Swipe Code</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In the time card, it will display the swipe code against the log in and log out time. The swipe codes are defined in the shift master, each swipe code is defined with <span class="GramE">In</span> and Out Time. While calculating the payroll, the application will consider the multiple swipes and calculate the working hours of the employee. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> Ex: Suppose in the shift master, the user has defined swipe code for lunch break as 13:00 – 15:00. When the employee log out and log in between those timings then in the time card it will be displayed as lunch break and timings of the swipes. </p><h4>Consider First In and Last Out</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is enabled, even though the employees did multiple swipes but then also the application will consider the first log in time and the last log out time while calculating the payroll. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138444"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.3</span></span>Monthly Payroll Attendance </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Options provided under this are related to calculation and approval of monthly payroll. </p><h4>Present Day for Attendance</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, it is reflected in the calculation of the payroll for the new employees that joins the company in the middle of the month. The application will consider the days the new employee has worked in that month. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> Suppose an employee joins the company on 15<sup>th</sup> Jan and the payroll is calculated at the end of the month. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> What happens when this checkbox is <b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">not checked</b>: The payroll will calculate the salary of the new employee only for 16 days. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> What happens when this checkbox is <b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">checked</b>: The payroll will calculate the salary of the new employee for 17 days. </p><h4>Allow Approval for Payroll</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, after calculating the payroll, it is not posted to the employees account instead it waits for the approval from the specific user. Unless the user authorizes the payroll, it is not posted to the employees account. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138445"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.4</span></span>Attendance for Weekly Offs &amp; Public Holiday </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> These options are provided to calculate the attendance with respect to weekly offs and public holidays, depending on the selections in this group, the application will generate the payroll for employees. </p><p class="MsoNormal">The options are as follows:</p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> 1.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">       </span></span></span>Automatic </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:42.55pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-2.85pt;mso-list:l2 level2 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> 1.1<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">             </span></span></span>Employee should be present for both previous and next day </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:4.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-4.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-17.0pt;mso-list:l2 level3 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">                                                  </span>1.1.1<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">            </span></span></span>Consider month end dates </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:4.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-4.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-17.0pt;mso-list:l2 level3 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">                                                  </span>1.1.2<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">            </span></span></span>Consider next month start date </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:42.55pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-2.85pt;mso-list:l2 level2 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> 1.2<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">             </span></span></span>Employee should be present either previous or next day </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:4.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-4.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-17.0pt;mso-list:l2 level3 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">                                                  </span>1.2.1<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">            </span></span></span>Consider month end dates </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:4.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;text-indent:-4.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-17.0pt;mso-list:l2 level3 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"><span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">                                                  </span>1.2.2<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">            </span></span></span>Consider next month start date </p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo10;"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> 2.<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">       </span></span></span>Manual </p><h4>Automatic</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the attendance is calculated automatically for all employees. After enabling the option, the user has to select either of the two options for considering weekly offs and public holidays. </p><p class="Style1">Employee should be present for both previous and next day</p><p class="MsoNormal"> If this option is checked, the employee need to be present for both previous and next day of the weekly offs and public holiday. If the employee is not present for both the previous and next day then the weekly offs and public holiday will be counted as absent. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Suppose 26<sup>th</sup> Jan – Thursday is a public holiday and if the employee is absent on Wednesday and Friday then the employee total absent count will be 3 days instead of 2 days because the employee was not present on the previous day of the public holiday and as well as the next day of the public holiday. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The same scenario is applied for weekly offs if the employee took holiday on Friday and Monday then the employees total absent count will be 4 days instead of 2 days. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the user has 1 more level of settings for this option to work efficiently. </p><p class="Style1">Employee should be present either previous or next day</p><p class="MsoNormal"> If this option is checked, the employee need to be present either previous or next day of the weekly offs and public holiday. If the employee is not present either previous or next day then the weekly offs and public holiday will be counted as absent. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Suppose 26<sup>th</sup> Jan – Thursday is a public holiday and if the employee took a leave on Wednesday then the employee total absent count will be 1 day instead of 2 days because the employee was present on the next day of the public holiday. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The same scenario is applied for weekly offs if the employee took leave on Friday then the employees total absent count will be 1 day. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the user gets 1 more level of settings for this option to work efficiently. </p><p class="Style1">Consider month end dates</p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will adjust the month end dates so as to accurately calculate the attendance of the employee. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Consider a scenario where the month is ending on weekend or on a public holiday then the application will adjust the month end date so as to calculate the attendance based on the setting. </p><p class="Style1">Consider next month start date</p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will adjust the next month start date so as to accurately calculate the attendance of the employee. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Consider a scenario where the month is ending on weekend or public holiday then the application will adjust the next month start date to calculate the attendance based on the setting. </p><h4>Manual</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the user has to manually enter the attendance for weekly offs and public holidays. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138446"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.5</span></span>Calendar </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> In this group, the user can select which calendar the application should follow. </p><h4>Calendar</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has the option to select which calendar to follow with the help of the radio buttons provided: </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>HCM Calendar </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this radio button is selected, attendance is calculated based on the calendar defined in the application. The user can define the calendar under Data Management tab. </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Focus Calendar </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this radio button is selected, the application considers the calendar defined in the Focus. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138447"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.6</span></span>Daily Payroll </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal">These options are related to daily payroll of the employee.</p><h4>Apply leave from daily payroll</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this is checked, leaves are applied while generating the daily payroll. </p><h4>Show absent status for non-leave pay groups</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, while generating the payroll for pay groups where leave is not defined i.e. non leave pay groups, it will show the status as absent for the employees of the pay group whenever they take a leave. </p><h4>Daily Payroll Entry Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has been provided with various options to be selected to enter the daily payroll. </p><p class="Style1" style="margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo11;"><span style="font-family:Wingdings;mso-fareast-font-family:Wingdings;mso-bidi-font-family:Wingdings;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> §<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;"> </span></span></span>Single Employee Single Day </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, payroll is calculated for single employee for a single day. </p><p class="Style1" style="margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo11;"><span style="font-family:Wingdings;mso-fareast-font-family:Wingdings;mso-bidi-font-family:Wingdings;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> §<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;"> </span></span></span>Single Employee Multiple Days </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, payroll is calculated for single employee for multiple days. </p><p class="Style1" style="margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo11;"><span style="font-family:Wingdings;mso-fareast-font-family:Wingdings;mso-bidi-font-family:Wingdings;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> §<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;"> </span></span></span>Multiple Employees Single Day </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, payroll is calculated for multiple employees for a single day. </p><p class="Style1" style="margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo11;"><span style="font-family:Wingdings;mso-fareast-font-family:Wingdings;mso-bidi-font-family:Wingdings;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> §<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;"> </span></span></span>Multiple Employees Multiple Days </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, payroll is calculated for multiple employees for multiple days. </p><h4>Auto Post Daily to Monthly</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> For all the above 4 settings for calculation of the daily payroll, the user has 1 more setting which can be enabled. When this option is checked, the daily attendance is posted automatically to monthly. Users do not have to manually go to “Post Full Attendance” screen and post the daily attendance to monthly. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> In the ESS, a “Submit” button is added when this option is checked. The employee at the end of the month has to click on the button for the application to automatically post daily attendance to monthly. </p><h4>Employee not to load</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> This option is enabled when either of the two multiple employees’ single day or multiple employees multiple days is checked. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, then in the daily payroll it will not load all details of the employee, the application will just calculate the daily payroll. </p><h4>Allow HOT/ WOT for all Days</h4><p class="MsoNormal">HOT means Holiday Overtime</p><p class="MsoNormal">WOT means <span class="GramE">Weekly</span> Overtime</p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, all the days in the calendar is considered as holiday overtime or weekly overtime. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138448"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.7</span></span>Convert Daily to Monthly </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Under this group, the user will find the settings for converting daily to monthly. </p><h4>Post Attendance</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will automatically convert the daily to monthly attendance and post the attendance. </p><h4>Post only auto increment leaves</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will post only the leaves which have been auto incremented for that specific period. It will not consider the attendance. </p><h4>Adjust Late against Leaves</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, whenever the employee comes after his log in time i.e. late to the office then as per the definition defined it will be adjusted against leave. The user will define how many late should be counted as a leave in the given fields: </p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-no-proof:yes;"></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"> In these textboxes, the user has to enter the number of late which will be adjusted against the number of leaves. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Consider the user has defined that 3 late is equal to 1 leave which means if the employee came late for 3 times then it is adjusted against his 1 day leave. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138449"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.8</span></span>Shift Assignment </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> In the “<b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;"> Shift Assignment </b>” screen the user will be assigning shifts to the Employees. </p><h4>Shift Assignment Entry Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> While assigning the shift, there is a date option in the “<b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">Shift Assignment</b>” screen where the user can select the date and assign the shifts. Depending on the selection in this group, the date option will be effected in the “<b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">Shift Assignment</b>” screen. </p>',106)),e("p",Gvs,[o[14]||(o[14]=e("span",{style:{"font-family":"Symbol","mso-fareast-font-family":"Symbol","mso-bidi-font-family":"Symbol","font-weight":"normal"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},[v(" ·"),e("span",{style:{font:'7.0pt "Times New Roman"'}},"         ")])],-1)),o[15]||(o[15]=v("Range")),e("span",Hvs,[s(c)])]),o[48]||(o[48]=e("p",{class:"MsoNormal"},[v(" When this option is checked, in the “"),e("b",{style:{"mso-bidi-font-weight":"normal"}},"Shift Assignment"),v("” screen the user need to select the date range to assign the shift. Shifts will be assigned based on the range selected. ")],-1)),e("p",qvs,[o[16]||(o[16]=e("span",{style:{"font-family":"Symbol","mso-fareast-font-family":"Symbol","mso-bidi-font-family":"Symbol","font-weight":"normal"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},[v(" ·"),e("span",{style:{font:'7.0pt "Times New Roman"'}},"         ")])],-1)),o[17]||(o[17]=v("Weekly")),e("span",Wvs,[s(c)])]),o[49]||(o[49]=e("p",{class:"MsoNormal"},[v(" When this option is checked, in the “"),e("b",{style:{"mso-bidi-font-weight":"normal"}},"Shift Assignment"),v("” screen the user need to select the week to assign the shift. Shifts will be assigned weekly to the employee. ")],-1)),e("p",zvs,[o[18]||(o[18]=e("span",{style:{"font-family":"Symbol","mso-fareast-font-family":"Symbol","mso-bidi-font-family":"Symbol","font-weight":"normal"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},[v(" ·"),e("span",{style:{font:'7.0pt "Times New Roman"'}},"         ")])],-1)),o[19]||(o[19]=v("Daily")),e("span",jvs,[s(c)])]),o[50]||(o[50]=Zo('<p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, in the “<b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">Shift Assignment</b>” screen the user need to select the day to assign the shift. Shifts will be assigned daily to the employee. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138450"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.9</span></span>Recruitment </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> All the options under this group are related to recruitment module. Recruiting involves a series of interviews with recruiters and at each level of interview the recruiter can either reject or pass the candidate to next level. </p><h4>Evaluation</h4><p class="Style1">Show candidate to all recruiters</p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the candidates will be visible to all recruiters even if the candidate is rejected. The recruiter will have a clear idea of how many candidates attended the interview and how many candidates have been assessed by the previous recruiter. </p><p class="Style1">Show candidate to all days</p><p class="MsoNormal"> Candidates are only visible to the recruiter on the day when the candidate has been called for an interview. Suppose the recruiter logs in the next day, in the dashboard he will only view the candidates of that day, for viewing next day he has to select the day from the calendar provided. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the candidates are visible to recruiters for all days. The user does not have to scroll to next day to view the candidates scheduled for that day. All the scheduled candidates for the coming days will be visible to recruiter. </p><h4>Agent Portal</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> An agent or a third party source is the person who will look for potential candidates whenever a new vacancy is posted by the company. They will be assisting the company in hiring a new employee as per their requirements. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> Agents will be given a URL portal and login credentials which is defined in the Source Master to access the new vacancy posted by the HR and apply for the position on behalf of the candidate. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The user will generate the URL by clicking on the “Get URL” button. </p><h4>Online Exam URL</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The Candidate will be given the URL and the Username and Password to login to the Online Exam portal to write the Exam. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The user can generate the URL by clicking the “Get URL” button and the Username and Password is defined in the Candidate screen in Recruitment Module. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The candidate goes to the URL and login with the provided credentials to write the exam. </p><h4>External Website</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> An external website can be a career page of the company or any other website where the candidate can view the jobs and apply. </p><p class="Style1">Candidate Layout</p>',21)),e("p",Yvs,[e("span",Jvs,[o[20]||(o[20]=v(" This option is provided to select the layout for candidates accessing the external website.")),s(c)])]),e("p",Kvs,[e("span",Qvs,[o[21]||(o[21]=v(" Candidate layout is defined in the “")),o[22]||(o[22]=e("b",{style:{"mso-bidi-font-weight":"normal"}},"Page Layout",-1)),o[23]||(o[23]=v("” screen.")),s(c)])]),o[51]||(o[51]=e("p",{class:"MsoNormal"},[e("span",{style:{"mso-no-proof":"yes"}},"Navigation: "),v("On the menu Click on "),e("b",{style:{"mso-bidi-font-weight":"normal"}},"Settings"),v(", Click "),e("em",null," Customization "),v("then Click"),e("em",null," on Recruitment "),v("then Click"),e("em",null," Candidate Layout"),v(" then Select "),e("em",null,"Page Layout"),v(". ")],-1)),e("p",Zvs,[e("span",Xvs,[o[24]||(o[24]=v("URL")),s(c)])]),e("p",eys,[e("span",tys,[o[25]||(o[25]=v(" The URL generated in this field is placed in the career page of the company. When any person clicks on this URL, it is redirected to the job description.")),s(c)])]),o[52]||(o[52]=e("h4",null,"Manpower Planning",-1)),e("p",lys,[e("span",ays,[o[26]||(o[26]=v(" Manpower Planning is the process of estimating or projecting the number of employees required over a predefined period of time. Planning can be done for department or location wise.")),s(c)])]),e("p",oys,[e("span",sys,[o[27]||(o[27]=v(" Earlier the user can plan for a specified period by selecting the date range. The user has the option to select with either of the radio buttons:")),s(c)])]),e("p",iys,[o[29]||(o[29]=e("span",{style:{"font-family":"Symbol","mso-fareast-font-family":"Symbol","mso-bidi-font-family":"Symbol","font-weight":"normal"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},[v(" ·"),e("span",{style:{font:'7.0pt "Times New Roman"'}},"         ")])],-1)),e("span",nys,[o[28]||(o[28]=v("Monthly")),s(c)])]),e("p",rys,[e("span",dys,[o[30]||(o[30]=v(" When this is selected, the user can plan manpower on monthly basis. The user can plan for each month.")),s(c)])]),e("p",uys,[o[32]||(o[32]=e("span",{style:{"font-family":"Symbol","mso-fareast-font-family":"Symbol","mso-bidi-font-family":"Symbol","font-weight":"normal"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},[v(" ·"),e("span",{style:{font:'7.0pt "Times New Roman"'}},"         ")])],-1)),e("span",cys,[o[31]||(o[31]=v("Yearly")),s(c)])]),e("p",pys,[e("span",mys,[o[33]||(o[33]=v(" When this is selected, the user can plan manpower on yearly basis. The user can plan for the whole year.")),s(c)])]),o[53]||(o[53]=Zo('<h4>Don’t consider Manpower Planning for Job Opening</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked by the user, monthly manpower planning defined in the “Manpower Planning” screen will not be considered while recruiting new candidates. The user can post the job opening without considering the manpower planning. </p><h4>Don’t consider Budgeting Manpower Planning</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, budget will not be considered in the manpower planning. The application will allow the user to plan the manpower without considering the budget defined in “Manpower Budget”. </p><h4>Don’t allow Back Dated Manpower Planning</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will not allow the user to save manpower planning for previous date i.e. date less than the current date. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138451"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.10</span></span>Job Description </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Under this group, the options provided are the selection of grades for the skill and appraisal. Grade is the Evaluation of the Candidates Performance. Grades will be defined in the “Grade” Master. The user also has to define the maximum and minimum value along with the weightage of the Grade. Grades are used in evaluating an employee’s performance. </p><h4>Skill Grade</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> This option is provided to select the standard grade for evaluating candidate’s performance in an interview. </p><h4>Appraisal Grade</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> This option is provided to select the standard grade for the appraisal. When the user selects a grade in this screen and saves then it is loaded in the “Job Grade” screen while defining the job grade for a particular position. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138452"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.11</span></span>Leaves </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> All the options under this are related to leave settings. Leave Types are defined in the preferences. </p><h4>LOP Leave</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user has the option to select the component for the leaves which are accounted as Loss of Pay (LOP). The components are defined in the Leaves Preferences. This component is used while calculating the payroll. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Suppose an employee has no leave balance but applied for a leave. This leave will go into the LOP Leave component selected here. </p><h4>Allow Negative Tolerance</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The employee can apply excess leaves and the negative leave balance will be accounted in the component defined for negative leave. When leaves are incremented, those leaves will be adjusted against the negative leave component selected in the next field. Generally at the end of the annum, the remaining excess leaves will be considered as loss of pay. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, it will allow the employees to apply negative leaves. </p><p class="MsoNormal">For Ex: An employee is assigned 15 annual leaves</p><p class="MsoNormal"> “Allow Excess Leaves” is <b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">not checked</b> – then the employee cannot apply leaves beyond the assigned limit. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> “Allow Excess Leaves” is <b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">checked</b> – then the employee can apply beyond 15 leaves and the remaining excess leave balance will go to negative leave type. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has the option to select the component which will allow excess leaves and negative leave balance in the below field. </p><h4>Leave Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has to select the leave component which will allow the employee to apply excess leaves. The leaves are consumed in this component first and rest of the leaves are accounted in the component selected in excess leave. </p><h4>Negative Leave Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has to select the component for negative leave balance. So whenever an employee leaves is negative in balance then those leaves are displayed against this selected component. </p><h4>COFF Leave Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> COFF is a compensatory leave, when an employee works over time, he can apply for COFF leave. The user has to select the component for compensatory leave which will be used in calculating the payroll. </p><h4>Allow Leaves after Payroll Calculation</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will allow the employees to raise leave application after the calculation of payroll. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138453"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.12</span></span>Training </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><h4>Training Grade</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> The user has to select the grade which will be used in assessing the employee’s performance after the training is completed. </p><h4>Training Plan Required</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In the “<b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal;">Training Plan</b>” screen, the user has to assign the Skills, Course, Trainer and Amount to each Employee who is going for Training. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, then it is mandatory for the user to define the training plan. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138454"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.13</span></span>Air Ticket </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><h4>Individual Family Tickets</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> By default, the employee and spouse are eligible for the air tickets. When this option is checked, the application will also allow the air tickets for the children of the employee. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138455"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.14</span></span>File System DB </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Under this group, all options are related to the application and database. </p><h4>URL</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user needs to enter the path to the server. </p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-no-proof:yes;"></span></p><h4>Application Path</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user needs to enter the path to the application. </p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-no-proof:yes;"></span></p><h4>Database Path</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user needs to enter the path to the database. </p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-no-proof:yes;"></span></p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138456"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.15</span></span></a><span class="SpellE"><span style="mso-bookmark:_Toc478138456;">Misc</span></span><span style="mso-bookmark:_Toc478138456;"></span></h2><h3>Description</h3><h4>Application URL</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In the field, the user has to enter the URL to access the application. </p><h4>Forgot Password Template</h4><h4>Date Format</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user has to select the date format to be followed across the application. </p><h4>ESS Credentials</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the employee credentials are picked from either of the selection: </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Employee Master </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this is selected, the application will consider the credentials defined in the employee master. </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>ESS Roles </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this is selected, the application will consider the credentials defined in the ESS roles when an employee logs in to the application. </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Active Directory </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this is selected, the application will consider the credentials stored in the active directory. When this is enabled, the user is provided with a text box to enter the Domain Name. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138457"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.16</span></span>Asset Clearance </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Options in this group are related to the assets when an employee is applying for a resignation. </p><h4>Need Clearance for Final Settlement</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application is required to consider the clearance of the asset i.e. whether the employee has returned the asset which was assigned to him. The process of clearance is performed while processing the final settlement in the “Employee Clearance” screen. </p><h4>Allow Resignation request before Days</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the application will restrict the employee from applying resignation based on the days entered in the below field: </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Before Days </p><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user has to enter the number of days before a request can be generated by the employee for the resignation. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138458"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.17</span></span>Organization Chart </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Organization chart is a graphical representation of the relation of one Employee to another in a company. </p><h4>Organization Chart Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> In this field, the user has the option to select the type of organization chart which the application should follow. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138459"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.18</span></span>Employee Asset Tags </a></h2><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138460"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.19</span></span>CTC Matrix </a></h2><h3>Description</h3><p class="MsoNormal"> Cost to Company (CTC) is a term used for the salary package of an employee. CTC matrix is merely depending on the working of each organization. The user can define the CTC matrix based on location, project or employee skills. The user will define many combinations of the calculation based on the tags selected in the screen. </p><h4>Consider CTC Matrix</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the CTC matrix defined in “Preferences” will be considered while calculating the payroll. The application will not consider the pay group when this is checked. </p><h2 style="mso-list:l4 level2 lfo1;"><a id="_Toc478138461"><span style="mso-fareast-font-family:Cambria;mso-fareast-theme-font:major-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Cambria;mso-bidi-theme-font:major-latin;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;">1.20</span></span>Payslip in ESS </a></h2>',93)),e("h3",null,[e("span",fys,[o[34]||(o[34]=v("Description")),s(c)])]),e("p",vys,[e("span",yys,[o[35]||(o[35]=v(" Payslip is given to an employee when they have been paid, detailing the amount of pay given, and the tax and insurance deducted.")),s(c)])]),o[54]||(o[54]=Zo('<h4>Type</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> This field is in regards to the viewing of back dated payslips in the ESS. The user has the option to select from the radio buttons. </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>Date Range </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the employee can view previously generated payslip based on the date range. The user has to select date range. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Suppose the date range selected is 1 Jan 2016 – 31 April 2016 </p><p class="MsoNormal"> In the month of March 2016, the employee can view backdated payslips up to Jan 2016. </p><p class="bullets" style="mso-list:l6 level1 lfo2;"><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;font-weight:normal;"><span style="mso-list:Ignore;"> ·<span style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">         </span></span></span>No. Of Months </p><p class="MsoNormal"> When this option is checked, the employee can view previously generated payslip based on the user entry in the text box. The text box is enabled only when this field is checked. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> For Ex: Suppose the user has entered 3 in the field then employee can view only 3 previously generated payslips. </p><h4>Password</h4><p class="MsoNormal"> When the payslip is sent to the employee via email, the file is password protected for security reasons. The user has to select the type of password in this field. The selected type will be used by the employee to open and view the file. </p><p class="MsoNormal"> Suppose password is selected as joining date. When the employee tries to open the file, he has to enter his joining date to view the file. </p><h4>Watermark</h4>',13)),e("p",hys,[e("span",gys,[o[36]||(o[36]=v(" A watermark is a translucent text to help prevent a file from being copied. In this field, the user can enter any text which will be used as watermark in the payslip.")),s(c)])]),e("h2",bys,[o[37]||(o[37]=e("a",{id:"_Toc478138462"},[e("span",{style:{"mso-fareast-font-family":"Cambria","mso-fareast-theme-font":"major-latin","mso-bidi-font-family":"Cambria","mso-bidi-theme-font":"major-latin"}},[e("span",{style:{"mso-list":"Ignore"}},"1.21")]),e("span",{style:{background:"white"}},"Roster")],-1)),e("span",Dys,[s(c)])]),o[55]||(o[55]=e("h3",null